    "text": "A body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup><mi>kg</mi></math> is moving in a medium and experiences a frictional force <math> <mrow> <mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>k</mi><msup> <mi>v</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>.</mo></mrow> </math> Its initial speed is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;After <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> its kinetic energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo></math> then value of <math> <mi>k</mi> </math> will be:-"
